<div class="mission" data-pagefind-body>

  <p class="mission-eyebrow">Mission</p>

  <h1 class="mission-lede">Atomdrift's Mission is to make supply-chain security
  <em class="mission-mark">accessible to the open-source community</em>,
  regardless of platform.</h1>

  <p class="mission-sub">We are driven by these principles:</p>

  <div class="principles">

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Local First</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Our tools will never require a cloud provider or remote AI
          endpoint, though they may use one if you ask.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Zero Telemetry</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Our tools never phone home. How you use them is your business,
          not ours.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Frugal</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Analysis is expensive, so we do it once and remember the
          answer.</li>
          <li>Human attention is even more expensive. Every false positive is
          a <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/scan/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">bug<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Portable</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Software runs everywhere, so security tools should too.</li>
          <li>We build and test on
          <a href="https://kernel.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Linux</a>,
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/macos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">macOS</a>,
          <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/windows" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Windows</a>,
          <a href="https://www.freebsd.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FreeBSD</a>, and
          <a href="https://illumos.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">illumos</a>;
          and provide best-effort support for all
          <a href="https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/platform-support.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tier&nbsp;1
          and Tier&nbsp;2 Rust platforms<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Composable</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Our tools produce output meant to be used by other tools.
          <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Integrations
          welcome<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Open</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Our tools and rules are
          <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apache&nbsp;2.0</a>
          and will stay that way.
          <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Patches
          welcome<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principle">
      <h2>Inspectable</h2>
      <div class="principle-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Every finding shows its work; otherwise it's just security
          theater.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <p class="mission-contact">Questions or patches?
  <a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
  or <span id="mission-mail">t, at this domain</span>.</p>

</div>

